From: Byron Campen <docfaraday@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:18:32 -0500
Subject: (tmp-cherry-pick) Revert "Allow combining AV1 SVC frames without
 dependency descriptor." (b67a9ce02b)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This reverts commit 52da778c185a17fe953ead983af213aa447e773e.

Reason for revert: Breaks downstream test

Failure Link: <LINK TO FAILURE>

Original change's description:
> Allow combining AV1 SVC frames without dependency descriptor.
>
> Although using scalability features with without Dependency Descriptors
> isn't a supported use case (falls outside the RTP Profile for AV1), it
> would help in some cases where the full stream is received (no sequence
> number gaps) and frames are otherwise detectable as complete (e.g. using
> the marker bit), to allow decoding SVC frames without knowing the actual
> spatial index.
>
> When receiving AV1 SVC without a dependency descriptor, PacketBuffer
> emits one RtpFrameObject per spatial layer and RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder
> verifies sequence number continuity across the temporal unit.
> RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder previously stamped SpatialIndex(0) onto every
> subframe, causing CombineAndDeleteFrames to reject multi-layer temporal
> units as having duplicate spatial indices.
>
> Leave SpatialIndex unset (std::nullopt) in RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder and
> only populate SpatialIndex and SpatialLayerFrameSize in
> CombineAndDeleteFrames when spatial indices are present. Also replace
> raw pointer arithmetic and memcpy in CombineAndDeleteFrames with
> std::span and std::ranges::copy.
>
> Bug: webrtc:560293075, chromium:569667447
